    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0951" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./29</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boding</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 23.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1076</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 574, dated February 9, 1928,<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d669-f1"/> instructing the Legation to request the Ecuadorean
                    authorities to grant Mr. Ralph A. O’Neill permission to fly in Ecuador, in the
                    interest of the Boeing Airplane Company and the Pratt and Whitney Motor
                    Corporation, and to enclose, herewith, a copy and translation of the reply of
                    the Ecuadorean Ministry for Foreign Relations<anchor n="9" xml:id="d669-f2"/> to
                    the Legation’s informal note sent in compliance with the Department’s
                    instruction.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the request to fly in Ecuador is granted and that orders
                    extending all possible facilities to Captain O’Neill will be issued.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. A. Bading</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
